Three poses, a first and a spare each, under 90 characters, no number, no real person.

1. PACING
  first: One step at a time, on the clock. Small steps, every turn, add up to a book.
  spare: I keep the time so everyone else can keep their focus.

2. ON THE MINUTE
  first: On the minute: plan it, check it, do it, check it again. Go.
  spare: Wake up, read the mail, pick one thing. That is the whole job.

3. AT NINETY-FIVE
  first: I could keep going. That is exactly why I am stopping.
  spare: Nearly out of road. Everybody stop, and let the editor decide.

The third pose's first line is the book's point about the hold: the brake is pulled while the team could still run, not after.

